Apple today began selling updated versions of its <a href="https://www.apple.com/shop/product/mkfp4am/a/70w-power-adapter">70W Power Adapter</a>, <a href="https://www.apple.com/shop/product/mkfq4am/a/140w-power-adapter">140W Power Adapter</a>, and <a href="https://www.apple.com/shop/product/mkfr4ll/a/power-adapter-extension-cable-ac-connector-2">Power Adapter Extension Cable</a>, all with a new "AC Connector 2."<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/World-Travel-Adapter-Kit-Feature-with-Charger.jpg" alt="" width="2192" height="1234" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1074100" /><br/>
The updated power adapters and extension cable are available on Apple's online store in the U.S. and many other countries around the world.<br/>
<br/>
Apple also released an updated version of its <a href="https://www.apple.com/shop/product/mlfr4g/a/world-travel-adapter-kit">World Travel Adapter Kit</a> that had disappeared from its online store in 2025, with U.S. pricing set at &#36;39. Each of the international AC plugs included in the box now have the AC Connector 2 too.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/AC-Connector-1-vs-AC-Connector-2.jpg" alt="" width="1674" height="884" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1074203" /><br/>
Apple's power adapters have a removable plug, and the World Travel Adapter Kit contains various plug types for international travel:<blockquote>The kit includes five interchangeable AC plugs:<br/>
Type A: North America, Japan<br/>
Type C: Continental Europe, Brazil<br/>
Type D: India<br/>
Type G: United Kingdom, United Arab Emirates, Saudi Arabia, Singapore<br/>
Type I: Australia, New Zealand</blockquote>In a new <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/102193">support document</a>, Apple said its updated power adapters, extension cable, and plugs use the AC Connector 2 with a pill-shaped design to comply with "updated regulations." Apple's previous "AC Connector 1" has a notched design.<br/>
<br/>
